   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE_13">via Sanità 2, III</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE">Trieste</name> (Italy)</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">The MS</seg> of <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">
                            <hi rend="underline">A</hi> <hi rend="underline">Portrait</hi> <hi rend="underline">of</hi> <hi rend="underline">the</hi> <hi rend="underline">Artist</hi> <hi rend="underline">as</hi> <hi rend="underline">a</hi> <hi rend="underline">Young</hi> <hi rend="underline">Man</hi>
                        </name> is safe and at your disposal. Shall I send it registered or keep it if you think the post still unsure. I am glad it is safe. Though my flat has been broken into I was relieved to find that my desk was untouched.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">                    	James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> <dateline>
                            <date when="1919-11-01">1/xi/919</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ mailed the manuscript to Harriet Weaver in <date when="1920-01">January 1920</date>, and in 1951 she donated it to the National Library of Ireland, where it remains. The Library has digitized the entire manuscript and it is available on the <rs type="external" key="https://catalogue.nli.ie/Record/vtls000359560">Library’s website</rs>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
